# Aipify Platform Business Language

**Aipify Platform shall use understandable business language.** Technical field names, raw database values, internal status codes, and developer terms must not be shown directly when a clear business term exists.

## Rules

1. Prefer business labels over technical identifiers in primary UI text.
2. Do not surface raw codes such as `slug`, `provisioning`, `payload`, `RPC`, `entitlement`, `app_subscription`, `license_type`, or `install_id` as primary labels.
3. Technical identifiers may appear in a secondary technical section when useful for administration, with a clear business label.
4. Map status and product codes through authoritative UI helpers before display.
5. Keep agreement duration separate from agreement status, and license package separate from registered users.

## Related

See also [aipify-global-platform.mdc](./aipify-global-platform.mdc) — Aipify is global by default.

## Platform Dashboard & navigation

Prefer business section labels in customer-facing Platform Admin UI:

- Operations → Drift (NO) / Operations (EN)
- Customers → Kunder
- Commercial → Avtaler og salg / Agreements & sales
- Knowledge → Kunnskap
- Product → Produkt
- Audit & Governance → Kontroll og styring / Control & governance
- Platform Dashboard → Platformoversikt / Platform overview
- Subscriptions → Kundeavtaler / Customer agreements
- Lifetime → Ubegrenset / Unlimited
- Deployments → Publiseringer / Publishing
- Platform Health → Plattformstatus / Platform status
- Data generated / response timestamps → Sist kontrollert / Last checked

Do not show raw deployment classification codes (`patch`, `minor`, `major`, `security`, `database_migration`) as primary UI text.
